  "splitter_line_differential_note": "StringWalker.php 250-251 is the only input-dependent branch: the root-level <?audit step=\"1\"?> PI in order-default-ns.xml takes the self-closing capture-once path and is returned as a node. StringWalker.php 18 and UniqueNode.php 19 are class declarations that run only on first load, which is the catalog-ns.xml run.",
  "source_reason": "StringWalker finds the next tag with preg_match('/<[^>]+>/'), classifies it by its opening and closing characters, adjusts a depth counter and copies input bytes until the capture depth is left. UniqueNode searches for '<name>' or '<name ' and the next '</name>' with preg_match and strpos. Neither reads names, attributes, text values or namespace declarations: getNode() returns verbatim input substrings, with entity and character references undecoded and prefixes whose declarations sit on the root left unbound. The README hands each node to simplexml_load_string for parsing; the package itself never calls an XML parser.",
  "parser_family": "none: own PCRE/strpos tag-boundary splitter; no ext/libxml, XMLReader, SimpleXML, DOM or ext/xml call in src/ (only the unreleased dev-xml-reader-parser branch name suggests XMLReader)",
  "docker_source_coverage": "run; both splitters and both stream routes executed under Xdebug on both controls",
  "afl_feedback": "not_run: the release runs no native XML parser, so libxml2 feedback would not come from this package; the package is PHP string and PCRE code whose output is a byte copy",
  "adapter": "lead-probes/php/xml/prewk_xml_string_streamer/probe.php",
  "recommended_lead_status": "excluded",
  "recommended_lead_reason": "Pinned 1.2.3 probe: getNode() returns verbatim input byte slices found by a preg_match/strpos tag-boundary splitter (StringWalker depth counter, UniqueNode name search); no names, attributes, decoded text or namespaces, and no XML parser call. Byte copying under PROTOCOL.md, not a parser. Evidence: data/php/xml/prewk-xml-string-streamer-lead-check.json."
